  "goodToKnow": "Die Sektion is a section or branch of an organisation: the local Sektion of the Alpenverein (Alpine Club) in Germany, Austria and Switzerland is a typical example. In medicine, it's an autopsy, and die Obduktion is the more common word. In Austria, Sektion is also a department of a ministry, headed by a Sektionschef. Don't mix it up with der Sekt (sparkling wine)."
